    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing high-ceiling matchups against soft opposing arms, specifically targeting the favorable conditions surrounding **James Wood** and **Tyler Soderstrom**. **James Wood** (74.75) is our premier play, leveraging an elite xwOBA of 0.430 and a prime lead-off spot against Freeland to capitalize on significant park factors. Meanwhile, both **Tyler Soderstrom** (70.82) and **Henry Bolte** (58.30) benefit from a juicy 7.04 xERA matchup against Bratt; while **Henry Bolte** is suppressed by his spot at the bottom of the order, **Tyler Soderstrom** offers superior efficiency in the two-hole. **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) also stands out as a strong play, as the combination of his platoon edge and a manageable matchup against Junk keeps him locked in our 3B slot.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Austin Riley** (63.87), who missed the cut by a razor-thin margin. While **Austin Riley** carries a solid projection, our optimizer leaned toward **Vinnie Pasquantino** (67.32) and **Josh Naylor** (64.04) due to their higher-floor consistency against their respective left-handed matchups. Elsewhere, **Brice Turang** (66.10) provides a sneaky boost to our SB-starved category; his matchup against Peralta is bolstered by a +4% efficiency lift due to the pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, making him a high-leverage start. We have intentionally benched **Travis Bazzana** and **Jose Caballero** as their sub-40 efficiency scores\u2014driven by difficult SP-matchups and poor placement in the batting order\u2014fall below our strict threshold for maintaining game caps. \n\nMonitor the status of **Zach McKinstry** (51.57), whose utility remains high despite the late-order usage, as his score is propped up by a positive wind factor against Taillon. Conversely, while **Cole Young** (55.06) presents as a marginal play against the tough profile of Abbott, we are sticking with the current configuration to maximize our platoon advantages. Ensure all lineups are finalized, as we are prioritizing efficiency over raw potential to keep our seasonal projections in line with the league\u2019s high-stakes SB requirements.",
